<title>POLAND: POLISH '97 RAPESEED HARVEST SEEN UP 20.9 PCT-GUS.</title>
<headline>POLISH '97 RAPESEED HARVEST SEEN UP 20.9 PCT-GUS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's rapeseed harvest this year will be at 543,100 tonnes, 20.9 percent higher than last year's 449,300 tonnes, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said in a preliminary estimate on Friday.</p>
<p>GUS said the estimation took into consideration damage from Poland's recent flood wave.</p>
<p>It said yields would be at 18 quintals per hectare.</p>
<p>GUS said that estimates from the first 10 days in July before the flooding began showed that about 585,000 tonnes would have been harvested with yields at 19.4 quintals per hectare.  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
